  %% @mode architecture
  %% @subtitle Who calls the stack, what runs inside the Docker host, and which services live outside it
  %% @card cyan | Clients | Browsers, SDKs, and agents reach the stack only through Traefik over HTTPS | API clients authenticate to LiteLLM with a virtual key or the master key | Operators use OpenSearch Dashboards, plus Grafana or Langfuse when enabled
  %% @card violet | Inside the stack | LiteLLM is the single gateway for models, search, MCP tools, and guardrails | Presidio, SearXNG, Xberg, PostgreSQL, and telemetry stay on internal networks | Every container log, metric, and trace lands in OpenSearch by default
  %% @card rose | Outside the stack | OpenAI serves completions; a separate GPU host runs D3-mini over TLS and dev BGE-M3 embeddings over plain HTTP | SearXNG scrapes public engines — review their terms of use | Xberg reaches only allowlisted sites through the Squid egress proxy
